<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
  Entitlements for the macrdp Camera CoreMediaIO system extension
  (camera redirection Phase 3). Used by packaging/make-camera-extension.sh when it
  signs the extension executable + bundle.

  A system extension MUST be app-sandboxed (CMIO launches it under a role account
  with a sandbox profile regardless). The App Group is what lets CMIO's
  CMIOExtensionMachServiceName resolve — the service name in camera-Info.plist is
  set byte-identical to this group id (the proven-safe form: it satisfies both the
  Team-ID-prefix and app-group-prefix rules at once).

  NO `com.apple.security.device.camera` here: this is a VIRTUAL camera fed decoded
  frames by macrdp — the extension never opens the Mac's physical camera — so the
  camera device entitlement is not needed (matches Apple's ldenoue/SinkCam sample,
  which omits it on the extension).

  The App Group id (__APP_GROUP__, substituted by the packaging script, e.g.
  QGLA89KHM7.com.clintcan.macrdp) MUST be registered in the Apple Developer portal
  and assigned to THIS extension's App ID (com.clintcan.macrdp.controller.camera).
  The container controller app does NOT need the group (it only activates the
  extension; the decoded-frame feed comes from macrdp.app via the CoreMediaIO
  client API, not an App-Group channel).
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.app-sandbox</key>
    <true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.application-groups</key>
    <array>
        <string>__APP_GROUP__</string>
    </array>
</dict>
</plist>
